description:
This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial items prepared in accordance with the format in FAR Part 12.&nbsp; This announcement constitutes the only solicitation.&nbsp; Quotations are being requested and a separate written solicitation will not be issued.&nbsp; 



Solicitation number 1240B27Q0025 is issued as a Request for Quotation (RFQ) for Research Triangle Park Forestry Sciences Laboratory HVAC Repair 



This acquisition&nbsp; is set-aside for small business concerns.&nbsp; The applicable North American Industry Classification Standard Code is 238220&nbsp; The small business size standard is $19 M&nbsp; This acquisition is a Total Small Business Set-Aside.&nbsp; All responsible sources may submit a quotation which will be considered by the agency.&nbsp; 



The primary HVAC system (ACCU-1/VRV 2-7) for the Forest Science and Assessment Center (FSAC) is a Mitsubishi VRF system (BHM06227, Model PURY-P120TLMU-A, Serial 79W00897, 10 tons, R-410A) with 6 interior units. The system does not maintain condition set points and an initial evaluation during a preventative maintenance service call diagnosed with a potentially significant refrigerant leak. 



The Forestry Science Laboratory (FSL) building&rsquo;s Fan Coil Units (FCUs) are redundant in the current HVAC system. The outside air vents are no longer needed and are introducing unconditioned air into the building. During cold weather, this can lead to the coils potentially freezing and have led to the freeze-stats tripping, resulting in nuisance shutdowns.
